From d529f00f98a4c5637b24d8e7cdf33095673006b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vigaz <pudimdebacon3@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 23:32:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: gki_defconfig: disable CFI_CLANG to match device
 modules

The device module tree (kernel_device_modules-6.6) already disables
CFI_CLANG via lamu_overlay.config, but the GKI kernel kept it enabled.
A CFI-instrumented kernel only accepts indirect calls into modules that
carry a matching CFI type id, so first-stage init died on the very first
module it loaded:

  init: Loading module /lib/modules/bootprof.ko with args ''
  CFI failure at do_one_initcall+0xd4/0x360
          (target: init_module+0x0/0xf7c [bootprof]; expected type: 0x36b1c5a6)
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Oops - CFI: Fatal exception

Captured from expdb on real hardware (moto g05/lamu, MT6769V/CB). The
kernel itself boots fine up to 'Run /init as init process' -- only the
module handoff fails.

Disabling on the kernel side is the permissive direction: a kernel built
without CFI loads both CFI and non-CFI modules, while the reverse is not
true. This also matters for the 434 prebuilt vendor blobs, which are
built against Motorola's own kernel and cannot be recompiled.
---
 arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
index 78048f40a8f6..5fd06cc417cb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
@@ -95,7 +95,6 @@ CONFIG_PTDUMP_STAGE2_DEBUGFS=y
 CONFIG_KPROBES=y
 CONFIG_JUMP_LABEL=y
 CONFIG_SHADOW_CALL_STACK=y
-CONFIG_CFI_CLANG=y
 CONFIG_MODULES=y
 CONFIG_MODULE_UNLOAD=y
 CONFIG_MODVERSIONS=y
-- 
2.55.0

